---
import Presentation from "../../../components/Presentation.astro";
import Divider from "../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a
          href="/courses/eng-design-fab/"
          class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3"
        >
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Session 4: Makerspace Safety I</h1>
        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <!-- Launch / Concept -->
        <section id="launch">
          <Presentation>
            <section>
              <h2>Session 4</h2>
              <h3 class="text-sn-theme">Makerspace Safety I</h3>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Some of You Are About to Meet a New Tool</h2>
              <p>
                Last session, we asked if your chosen concept needs a tool or
                material you haven't used before.
              </p>
              <p class="fragment">
                Before anyone touches anything in this room, we cover how to
                stay safe doing it.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>Safety Isn't a Footnote</h2>
              <p>
                In this course, safety is a <b class="text-sn-theme"
                  >graded competency</b
                >, the same as measurement or documentation.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>Safety Isn't a Footnote</h2>
              <p>
                Not a one-time lecture you sit through and forget. Something
                you're expected to actually demonstrate.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Two Safety Sessions</h2>
              <ul>
                <li class="fragment"><b>Today:</b> recognizing hazards across the whole shop</li>
                <li class="fragment">
                  <b>Next time:</b> hands-on certification on the specific
                  tools you'll actually use
                </li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>Hazard + Practice, Paired</h2>
              <p>Every hazard in this room has a matching safe practice.</p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>Hazard + Practice, Paired</h2>
              <p>
                You don't need to memorize a list. You need to be able to <b
                  class="text-sn-theme">recognize a hazard</b
                > and name what you'd actually do about it.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Hazard Categories You'll See Today</h2>
              <ul>
                <li class="fragment">Sharp edges &amp; blades</li>
                <li class="fragment">Moving parts &amp; pinch points</li>
                <li class="fragment">Dust &amp; debris</li>
                <li class="fragment">Noise</li>
                <li class="fragment">Electrical</li>
                <li class="fragment">Walkways &amp; clutter</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Today's Activity: Shop Walkthrough</h2>
              <p>
                In small groups, tour the makerspace. At each station your
                instructor points out, identify the hazard and the matching
                safe practice.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>What You're Graded On</h2>
              <p>Not a written test.</p>
              <p class="fragment">
                Engagement during the walkthrough, and being able to restate
                <b class="text-sn-theme">one hazard/practice pair</b> in your
                own words when asked.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate data-auto-animate-restart>
              <h2>Two Things to Remember</h2>
              <p><b class="text-sn-theme">Safety isn't a memorized list.</b></p>
              <p class="fragment">
                It's recognizing a hazard in context &mdash; the same room can
                be safe or unsafe depending on what you're doing in it.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section data-auto-animate>
              <h2>Two Things to Remember</h2>
              <p><b class="text-sn-theme">If you don't know, ask before you touch it.</b></p>
              <p class="fragment">
                Every single time. No exceptions, no matter how simple it
                looks.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Next Time</h2>
              <p>Session 5: Makerspace Safety II</p>
              <p class="fragment">
                Hands-on demonstrations and a certification quiz on the
                specific tools you'll need.
              </p>
            </section>
          </Presentation>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Build -->
        <section id="build">
          <h2>Build</h2>

          <p>
            Today's "build" is the walkthrough itself. At each station your
            instructor points out, fill in the hazard and the matching safe
            practice.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Worked Example</h3>
          <table class="table table-dark table-sm">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Station</th>
                <th>Hazard</th>
                <th>Safe Practice</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Table saw</td>
                <td>Spinning blade can't tell your fingers from the material</td>
                <td>
                  Push stick for narrow cuts, hands always clear of the
                  blade's path, blade guard stays on
                </td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>Your Walkthrough Checklist</h3>
          <p>For each category, name the station where you saw it and the matching practice:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Sharp edges &amp; blades</li>
            <li>Moving parts &amp; pinch points</li>
            <li>Dust &amp; debris</li>
            <li>Noise</li>
            <li>Electrical</li>
            <li>Walkways &amp; clutter</li>
          </ul>

          <p>
            You don't need a hazard for every category if your instructor
            didn't point one out &mdash; but you do need at least <b
              class="text-sn-theme">three complete pairs</b
            > by the end of the walkthrough.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Checkpoint -->
        <section id="checkpoint">
          <h2>Checkpoint</h2>

          <p>
            Before you move on, close your notes and check yourself: can you
            restate <b>one</b> hazard/practice pair from today, out loud, in
            your own words &mdash; not read off the page?
          </p>

          <p>
            If you can't, pick your clearest pair and re-walk it in your head:
            what's the hazard, specifically, and what's the one thing you'd
            actually do differently because of it?
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Reflection -->
        <section id="reflection">
          <h2>Reflection</h2>

          <p>Answer the following questions before submitting your work.</p>

          <ol>
            <li>
              Pick one hazard/practice pair from today. Write both in your
              own words &mdash; not copied from the board.
            </li>
            <li>
              Which station's hazard surprised you most &mdash; something you
              wouldn't have flagged as risky before today?
            </li>
            <li>
              Look back at your Session 3 concept sketches &mdash; which
              specific tool or machine does your chosen concept depend on
              most? Session 5 is where you'll get certified on tools like it.
            </li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Submit -->
        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>Submit your walkthrough checklist and your reflection.</p>

          <h1
            class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
          >
            Activity Complete
          </h1>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
